s.ie\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/ActivPanel-demo-300x200.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Irish schools are changing \u2014 and so are their classrooms. With digital transformation at the heart of modern education, more and more schools across Ireland are replacing old tools like chalkboards and projectors with a smarter solution: the interactive whiteboard. Today\u2019s interactive whiteboards are large-format touchscreen displays, designed for collaborative learning, real-time annotation, and wireless sharing. They\u2019re helping schools boost engagement, streamline teaching, and prepare students for a tech-driven world. Let\u2019s explore why interactive touchscreens \u2014 commonly known as interactive whiteboards \u2014 are becoming the standard in Irish primary and secondary schools. What Is an interactive whiteboard? An interactive whiteboard is a digital display (usually 65\u201386 inches) that works like a giant tablet. It allows teachers and students to: Write, draw, and annotate on-screen Open and interact with educational apps Display and control lessons from a laptop, USB, or the cloud Use built-in tools like timers, graphing, and split-screen Enable student interaction at the board Unlike traditional projectors, these screens offer: No shadows No bulbs Ultra-clear 4K resolution True multi-touch support All-in-one, plug-and-play simplicity At Interactive Displays Ireland, we supply interactive whiteboards with advanced features and long warranties, purpose-built for Irish classrooms. Why Irish Schools Are Making the Switch 1. Better Engagement = Better Learning Students learn best when they\u2019re engaged. The interactive whiteboard transforms passive lessons into interactive experiences: Students can come up and answer questions by touch Teachers can use real-time drawing, video, and apps Lessons become visual, dynamic, and more memorable \ud83d\udcca Stat: According to a UK study, classrooms using interactive displays saw a 16% improvement in student performance compared to traditional whiteboards. 2. Modern Tools for Modern Learners Today\u2019s students grow up using smartphones and tablets \u2014 they expect the same interactivity in the classroom. Interactive whiteboards bridge that gap: Compatible with Google Classroom, Microsoft Teams, and Seesaw Enable wireless screen sharing from iPads, Chromebooks, or laptops Support educational apps like Kahoot!, GeoGebra, and Scratch Teachers can integrate video, websites, and cloud tools into any lesson \u2014 from maths to Gaeilge. 3. More Teaching, Less Tech Trouble Unlike old projector setups, interactive whiteboards don\u2019t need calibration, bulb replacements, or speakers. Most are all-in-one units with: Built-in Android OS or Windows PC Touch-enabled whiteboarding apps HDMI, USB, and wireless connectivity This saves teachers time and reduces IT headaches. Real Feedback From Irish Classrooms Here\u2019s what some of our clients had to say after upgrading to interactive whiteboards: \ud83c\udfeb \u201cWe replaced our old Promethean board with a 75\u201d interactive touchscreen from Interactive Displays. The image quality is stunning and our teachers love how simple it is to use. No more delays at the start of class.\u201d \u2013 Principal, Primary School in Meath \ud83d\udcda \u201cOur students are more involved in lessons and the ability to wirelessly cast from their Chromebooks has changed the way we teach group work.\u201d \u2013 Secondary Teacher, Dublin How It Helps Teachers No downtime: Instant-on, no warm-up Built-in tools: Rulers, protractors, split-screen, timers Record lessons: Save and share content after class Collaboration: Up to 20 students can interact at once Many teachers even use the interactive whiteboard to run quizzes, play educational games, or bring in YouTube videos for visual learning. Funding Support for Schools The Irish Department of Education continues to support digital infrastructure in schools through grant schemes and digital strategy rollouts. Interactive whiteboards fall under approved IT and AV equipment categories. Need help with quotes or specs for tenders? Interactive Displays Ireland provides full support, including: WEEE-certified removal of old screens Professional installation nationwide CPD teacher training available School-specific pricing with warranty Why Choose Interactive Displays Ireland? We\u2019ve supplied and installed interactive whiteboards for schools across Ireland since 2009 \u2014 from small rural classrooms to large secondary campuses. Here\u2019s what sets us apart: \u00a0Trusted brands like Vestel, Moytronix, and CleverTouch\u00a0Tailored quotes for individual schools or full upgradesOn-site demos and remote training available\u00a0Content control via our optional platform, screenfusion.ai Whether you\u2019re upgrading one classroom or 20, we\u2019ll help you choose the right screen size, spec, and software \u2014 with no jargon or upselling. Common Questions from Schools Q: Do we need a separate computer to run it? A: No. Most of our interactive whiteboards include built-in Android OS and optional Windows PC modules. You can also connect your existing laptop or device. Q: What size is best for a classroom? A: We recommend: 65\u201d\u201375\u201d for small to medium classrooms 75\u201d\u201386\u201d for larger rooms or high visibility needs Q: Do you provide training? A: Yes \u2014 every install includes basic training, and CPD training sessions are available for larger rollouts. Conclusion The interactive whiteboard is quickly becoming an essential tool in modern Irish classrooms. With better engagement, fewer technical issues, and seamless integration with digital learning platforms, it\u2019s no surprise that schools are making the switch. Whether you\u2019re a teacher, principal, or ICT coordinator, upgrading your classroom with an interactive whiteboard is an investment in both your staff and students. \ud83c\udf93 Ready to upgrade your classroom? Contact InteractiveDisplays.ie for a free consultation or explore short-term trials and flexible options tailored for Irish schools. Also check out: screenfusion.ai for remote content control rentascreen.ie for temporary display rentals<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":329,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1498","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1498","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/2"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1498"}],"version-history":[{"count":8,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1498\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1506,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1498\/revisions\/1506"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/329"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1498"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.ie\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=1498"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.interactivedisplays.i